kelixip (1.6.4-2) stable; urgency=low

  * New package kelixip-mod-sip-servers: the remote SIP servers of a domain
    (sip-appsrv, sip-proxy, sip-trunk), declared with kelictl sip_servers,
    the REST API or kelescope and kept in server_file. Scripts call
    matches_server/2, find_server/2 and forward/3; a [module.sip_servers] block
    in config.toml enables it.
  * Each server's URIs are probed by OPTIONS; a call skips a URI known to be
    down. A request from a server that a script recognises proves it alive:
    its OPTIONS reach a script through a [[domain.options]] rule.
  * A sip-trunk registers its account (register = true by default) and answers
    the operator's 401/407 on INVITE, re-INVITE, UPDATE, BYE and MESSAGE with
    its HA1; the password is never stored.
  * A sip-proxy's remote AORs are probed through it and reported to presence.
  * kelescope 0.7.0 shows a domain's servers live: subscribe_sip_servers/2
    pushes each server's state, counters and alarms (realm mismatch, address
    shared by two servers).
  * A script can keep an inbound P-Asserted-Identity: trust_asserted_identity/1.
  * Digest: a challenge naming SHA-256, the RFC 8760 spelling, is answered.

 -- Emmanuel BUU <emmanuel.buu@ives.fr>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200

kelixip (1.6.4-1) stable; urgency=low

  * Screen sharing through the B2BUA. A leg carries several video streams
    and BUNDLE: the second m=video of a browser sharing its screen is a stream
    of its own, relayed to the other leg under its mid; a share that stops is
    paused (inactive), not withdrawn, so sharing again resumes it; a re-offer
    keeps the peer's section order and the leg's ICE credentials.
  * Security incidents for fail2ban. A refused credential, an unknown domain,
    a refused API token, a packet that is not SIP or a failed handshake is one
    line in [security] log_file (default /var/log/kelixip/security.log) and
    in the journal. Filters and a jail example are installed under
    /usr/share/kelixip/fail2ban/; /etc/logrotate.d/kelixip rotates the file.
    [security] ignore drops incident types.
  * The SIP parser accepts header names in any case, the compact forms and a
    colon without a space after it (RFC 3261 section 7.3).
  * The reference media call script carries text too (T.140 data channel).
  * User-Agent is now Kelixip/1.6.4.

 -- Emmanuel BUU <emmanuel.buu@ives.fr>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200

kelixip (1.6.3-2) stable; urgency=low

  * RFC 4028 session timers, one per call leg. A long call relayed between two
    browsers was cut after 90 s: the caller's Session-Expires was relayed to
    the callee, who then waited for kelixip to refresh its leg.
    Session-Expires, Min-SE and the `timer` option tag no longer cross a B2BUA.
  * Every call leg negotiates its own timer with its own peer, refreshes it
    (UPDATE, or re-INVITE for a peer without UPDATE) when it is the refresher,
    and hangs up a peer that stops refreshing (Reason: 408 Session Timer
    Expired). Scripts using bridge() receive {:bridge, :session_expired, ...}.
  * New [session_timer] section in config.toml: enabled (default true),
    expires (1800), min_se (90), refresher (local | remote, default local).

 -- Emmanuel BUU <emmanuel.buu@ives.fr>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200

kelixip (1.6.3-1) stable; urgency=low

  * Presence: the composite person keeps the extension elements a client puts
    in <rpid:activities> beside its activity (Trix's <trix:dnd/> and
    <trix:auto/>). Lost until now, a Trix watching its own presence read
    "do not disturb" back as busy and kept busy after a reload.
  * User-Agent is now Kelixip/1.6.3.

 -- Emmanuel BUU <emmanuel.buu@ives.fr>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0200

kelixip (1.6.2-1) stable; urgency=low

  * Basic instant messaging (page mode, RFC 3428): a [[domain.chat]] block routes
    a MESSAGE to the `chat` function; a MESSAGE's content is never logged.
  * Conversations: one scenario handles every MESSAGE of a conversation, keyed on
    its flow; an idle conversation hibernates and is woken by the next MESSAGE.
  * New package kelixip-mod-conversation keeps hibernated conversations in SQL,
    so one hibernated on a node wakes on another and survives a restart.
  * New package kelixip-mod-silo: store-and-forward in SQL. A MESSAGE no device
    took is stored and delivered when one of the recipient's devices registers;
    kelictl silo list|purge.
  * SBB.Page relays one MESSAGE to every device of the recipient in parallel.
  * Reference scripts p2p-chat.exs and registrar-chat.exs.
  * Kelix.DB.Pool: the SQL link shared by every SQL module; an optional
    [database] block in config.toml supplies driver, host, port and TLS.
  * kelictl shows an inactivity column for hibernated scenarios.
  * The control API encodes a pid as text: GET /scenarios no longer answers 500.
  * User-Agent is now Kelixip/1.6.2.

 -- Emmanuel BUU <emmanuel.buu@ives.fr>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0200

